{
  "_doc": "Which detailed (Meshy) model each hazard uses in first person: assets/models/<model>.glb. 'painters' maps a drawing style to a model; 'hazards' picks one per hazard id (and wins). length: share of the hazard's length the model fills; tint multiplies the model's colours (for a related species); yaw turns the model to face +X; fit 'x' measures across +X after the turn (wingspan for birds); bob: stride bounce; sink: how deep it sits (floating backs); hop: a kangaroo's bound height instead of a stride; fur: colours for a model that came without a texture (top, belly, dark). A model that hasn't been made yet just leaves the old shape in place. See docs/CONTENT.md. 'scenery' maps a first-person scenery prop or landmark ('lm_<kind>') to a model and its height in tiles; 'open_trees' and 'open_plants' are what grows beside the open (sunny) rows. align 'long' turns a model so its longest side runs along +X (logs, vehicles). 'animals' gives an animal its model for the home and animal screens. 'edge' lines the far edges of the open rows (every other row).",
